IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `types`
IMPORT `chapter-3-punishments`

§ `The standalone punishment sections`

-- Penal Code 1871 ss 302, 304, 311, 323, 325, 341, 342, 363, 363A, 379, 379A, 384,
-- 392, 395, 406, 417, 419, 426, 447, 448, 458A, 465, 500, 512.
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt.
--
-- The Code separates some offences into a defining section and a punishing section:
-- s 300 says what murder is and s 302 what it is punished with; s 378 and s 379; s 463
-- and s 465. Until 15 Sep 2026 this subject encoded the defining sections and left
-- the punishing ones out, on the policy that it does not compute sentence. That
-- policy stands -- nothing here is a sentence -- but the punishing sections are law
-- too, and the Chapter 3 vocabulary already says what they say: the ceiling, and
-- where the Code fixes one the floor, that the section makes available. This module
-- gives each of them a rule in that vocabulary.
--
-- Most are constants: "whoever commits theft shall be punished with imprisonment
-- for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both" is one
-- `Punishment`. Six turn on a fact: s 302 on which limb of s 300 the murder falls
-- under, s 304 on the s 299 intention, s 379A on the thing stolen being a motor
-- vehicle, s 392 on the hour, s 458A on a previous conviction, s 512 on the offence
-- attempted and whether express provision is made. ss 302 and 304 take the Homicide
-- record, since the facts are already on it; the others take a small record of
-- their own, declared here as `Aggravation Facts` is in chapter-3-punishments.l4.
--
-- The punishment sections of the Chapters newly encoded on 15 Sep -- ss 130E, 143,
-- 147, 193, 267B, 290, and ss 109 to 120 -- are in their own Chapter modules.

§§ `The facts the punishment sections turn on`

DECLARE `Sentencing Facts` HAS
    -- Section 379A
    `the property stolen is a motor vehicle or a component part of a motor vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- Section 392
    `the robbery is committed after 7 pm and before 7 am` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- Section 458A
    `the offender has previously been convicted of an offence under section 449 450 451 or 452` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- Section 512
    `the offence attempted is punishable with death or imprisonment for life` IS A BOOLEAN
    `express provision is made by this Code or by the other written law for the punishment of the attempt` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Chapter 16 -- Sections 302, 304, 311, 323, 325, 341, 342, 363 and 363A`

-- s 302(1): murder within s 300(a) -- the act done with the intention of causing
-- death -- is punished with death. s 302(2): murder within s 300(b), (c) or (d) is
-- punished with death or imprisonment for life, and caning if not death. The s 300
-- limb facts are on the Homicide record; the rule tests limb (a) and treats any
-- other murder as (b), (c) or (d).

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 302"
@export Give the punishment for murder under Penal Code 1871 section 302
GIVEN hm IS A Homicide @desc The homicide facts. Death is mandatory for a s 300(a) murder; otherwise death or imprisonment for life, with caning if not death.
GIVETH A Punishment
DECIDE `the punishment for murder` hm IS
    IF hm's `the act by which the death is caused is done with the intention of causing death`
    THEN `death only`
    ELSE `death or imprisonment for life and liable to caning`

-- s 304(a): the act done with the intention of causing death, or of causing such
-- bodily injury as is likely to cause death -- imprisonment for life and caning, or
-- up to 20 years and fine or caning. s 304(b): done with the knowledge that it is
-- likely to cause death but without either intention -- up to 15 years, or fine, or
-- caning, or any combination.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 304"
@export Give the punishment for culpable homicide not amounting to murder under Penal Code 1871 section 304
GIVEN hm IS A Homicide @desc The homicide facts. Life or up to 20 years with fine or caning where the act was done with the intention of causing death or of causing bodily injury likely to cause death; otherwise up to 15 years, fine, caning or any combination.
GIVETH A Punishment
DECIDE `the punishment for culpable homicide not amounting to murder` hm IS
    IF      hm's `with the intention of causing death`
        OR  hm's `with the intention of causing such bodily injury as is likely to cause death`
    THEN `imprisonment for life or up to and liable to fine or caning` 20
    ELSE `imprisonment up to and liable to fine or caning or both` 15

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 311"
@export Give the punishment for infanticide under Penal Code 1871 section 311
GIVETH A Punishment
`the punishment for infanticide` MEANS `imprisonment for life or up to and liable to fine` 10

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 323"
@export Give the punishment for voluntarily causing hurt under Penal Code 1871 section 323
GIVETH A Punishment
`the punishment for voluntarily causing hurt` MEANS `imprisonment up to or fine up to or both` 3 5000

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 325"
@export Give the punishment for voluntarily causing grievous hurt under Penal Code 1871 section 325
GIVETH A Punishment
`the punishment for voluntarily causing grievous hurt` MEANS `imprisonment up to and liable to fine or caning or both` 10

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 341"
@export Give the punishment for wrongful restraint under Penal Code 1871 section 341
GIVETH A Punishment
`the punishment for wrongful restraint` MEANS `imprisonment up to or fine up to or both` (1 DIVIDED BY 12) 1500

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 342"
@export Give the punishment for wrongful confinement under Penal Code 1871 section 342
GIVETH A Punishment
`the punishment for wrongful confinement` MEANS `imprisonment up to or fine or both` 3

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 363"
@export Give the punishment for kidnapping under Penal Code 1871 section 363
GIVETH A Punishment
`the punishment for kidnapping` MEANS `imprisonment up to and liable to fine or caning or both` 10

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 363A"
@export Give the punishment for abduction under Penal Code 1871 section 363A
GIVETH A Punishment
`the punishment for abduction` MEANS `imprisonment up to and liable to fine or caning or both` 7

§§ `Chapter 17 -- Sections 379, 379A, 384, 392, 395, 406, 417, 419, 426, 447, 448 and 458A`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 379"
@export Give the punishment for theft under Penal Code 1871 section 379
GIVETH A Punishment
`the punishment for theft` MEANS `imprisonment up to or fine or both` 3

-- s 379A: theft of a motor vehicle or a component part of one -- up to 7 years and
-- fine. Where the thing stolen is not a motor vehicle the section has nothing to
-- say and the rule gives s 379's punishment. s 379A(2), disqualification from
-- driving, is an order and not a punishment within s 53; it is not carried.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 379A"
@export Give the punishment for theft of a motor vehicle under Penal Code 1871 section 379A
GIVEN sf IS A `Sentencing Facts` @desc Whether the thing stolen is a motor vehicle or a component part of one. If not, the s 379 punishment.
GIVETH A Punishment
DECIDE `the punishment for theft of a motor vehicle` sf IS
    IF sf's `the property stolen is a motor vehicle or a component part of a motor vehicle`
    THEN `imprisonment up to and liable to fine` 7
    ELSE `the punishment for theft`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 384"
@export Give the punishment for extortion under Penal Code 1871 section 384
GIVETH A Punishment
`the punishment for extortion` MEANS `imprisonment from to and liable to caning` 2 7

-- s 392: 2 to 10 years and caning of not less than 6 strokes; after 7 p.m. and
-- before 7 a.m., 3 to 14 years and not less than 12 strokes.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 392"
@export Give the punishment for robbery under Penal Code 1871 section 392
GIVEN sf IS A `Sentencing Facts` @desc Whether the robbery was committed after 7 p.m. and before 7 a.m.
GIVETH A Punishment
DECIDE `the punishment for robbery` sf IS
    IF sf's `the robbery is committed after 7 pm and before 7 am`
    THEN `imprisonment from to and caning of not less than strokes` 3 14 12
    ELSE `imprisonment from to and caning of not less than strokes` 2 10 6

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 395"
@export Give the punishment for gang-robbery under Penal Code 1871 section 395
GIVETH A Punishment
`the punishment for gang-robbery` MEANS `imprisonment from to and caning of not less than strokes` 5 20 12

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 406"
@export Give the punishment for criminal breach of trust under Penal Code 1871 section 406
GIVETH A Punishment
`the punishment for criminal breach of trust` MEANS `imprisonment up to or fine or both` 7

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 417"
@export Give the punishment for cheating under Penal Code 1871 section 417
GIVETH A Punishment
`the punishment for cheating` MEANS `imprisonment up to or fine or both` 3

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 419"
@export Give the punishment for cheating by personation under Penal Code 1871 section 419
GIVETH A Punishment
`the punishment for cheating by personation` MEANS `imprisonment up to or fine or both` 5

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 426"
@export Give the punishment for mischief under Penal Code 1871 section 426
GIVETH A Punishment
`the punishment for mischief` MEANS `imprisonment up to or fine or both` 2

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 447"
@export Give the punishment for criminal trespass under Penal Code 1871 section 447
GIVETH A Punishment
`the punishment for criminal trespass` MEANS `imprisonment up to or fine up to or both` (3 DIVIDED BY 12) 1500

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 448"
@export Give the punishment for house-breaking under Penal Code 1871 section 448
GIVETH A Punishment
`the punishment for house-breaking` MEANS `imprisonment up to or fine or both` 3

-- s 458A: a person previously convicted under s 449, 450, 451 or 452 who commits
-- another such offence is liable to caning in addition to the punishment prescribed
-- for it. The rule takes that prescribed punishment and adds caning.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 458A"
@export Give the punishment for a subsequent offence under Penal Code 1871 section 449, 450, 451 or 452, under section 458A
GIVEN sf IS A `Sentencing Facts` @desc Whether the offender has a previous conviction under s 449, 450, 451 or 452.
      p IS A Punishment @desc The punishment prescribed for the s 449, 450, 451 or 452 offence now committed.
GIVETH A Punishment
DECIDE `the punishment for a subsequent house-breaking offence` sf p IS
    IF sf's `the offender has previously been convicted of an offence under section 449 450 451 or 452`
    THEN `with caning added` p
    ELSE p

§§ `Chapters 18 and 21 -- Sections 465 and 500`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 465"
@export Give the punishment for forgery under Penal Code 1871 section 465
GIVETH A Punishment
`the punishment for forgery` MEANS `imprisonment up to or fine or both` 4

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 500"
@export Give the punishment for defamation under Penal Code 1871 section 500
GIVETH A Punishment
`the punishment for defamation` MEANS `imprisonment up to or fine or both` 2

§§ `Chapter 23 -- Section 512, punishment for attempts`

-- s 512(1): an attempt to commit an offence punishable with death or imprisonment
-- for life, where no express provision is made for the attempt's punishment -- up to
-- 20 years, and liable to fine or caning. The Illustration is an attempted
-- kidnapping in order to murder.
-- s 512(2): any other attempt, where no express provision is made -- the punishment
-- prescribed for the offence, subject to s 512(3): a fixed, specified minimum or
-- mandatory minimum sentence does not bind the court, which may pass any sentence up
-- to the maximum. s 512(4): no type of punishment not prescribed for the offence.
-- Where express provision IS made, s 512 says nothing, and the rule says so with
-- `no punishment prescribed`: the caller must look to that provision.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 512"
@export Give the punishment for attempting to commit an offence under Penal Code 1871 section 512
GIVEN sf IS A `Sentencing Facts` @desc Whether the offence attempted is punishable with death or life, and whether express provision is made for the attempt's punishment.
      p IS A Punishment @desc The punishment prescribed for the offence attempted.
GIVETH A Punishment
DECIDE `the punishment for an attempt` sf p IS
    IF sf's `express provision is made by this Code or by the other written law for the punishment of the attempt`
    THEN `no punishment prescribed`
    ELSE (IF sf's `the offence attempted is punishable with death or imprisonment for life`
          THEN `imprisonment up to and liable to fine or caning or both` 20
          ELSE `with no minimum sentence` p)

§§ `Illustrations`

`no sentencing facts` MEANS `Sentencing Facts` WITH
    `the property stolen is a motor vehicle or a component part of a motor vehicle` IS FALSE
    `the robbery is committed after 7 pm and before 7 am` IS FALSE
    `the offender has previously been convicted of an offence under section 449 450 451 or 452` IS FALSE
    `the offence attempted is punishable with death or imprisonment for life` IS FALSE
    `express provision is made by this Code or by the other written law for the punishment of the attempt` IS FALSE

`a night robbery` MEANS `Sentencing Facts` WITH
    `the property stolen is a motor vehicle or a component part of a motor vehicle` IS FALSE
    `the robbery is committed after 7 pm and before 7 am` IS TRUE
    `the offender has previously been convicted of an offence under section 449 450 451 or 452` IS FALSE
    `the offence attempted is punishable with death or imprisonment for life` IS FALSE
    `express provision is made by this Code or by the other written law for the punishment of the attempt` IS FALSE

`a stolen car` MEANS `Sentencing Facts` WITH
    `the property stolen is a motor vehicle or a component part of a motor vehicle` IS TRUE
    `the robbery is committed after 7 pm and before 7 am` IS FALSE
    `the offender has previously been convicted of an offence under section 449 450 451 or 452` IS FALSE
    `the offence attempted is punishable with death or imprisonment for life` IS FALSE
    `express provision is made by this Code or by the other written law for the punishment of the attempt` IS FALSE

`a repeat house-breaker` MEANS `Sentencing Facts` WITH
    `the property stolen is a motor vehicle or a component part of a motor vehicle` IS FALSE
    `the robbery is committed after 7 pm and before 7 am` IS FALSE
    `the offender has previously been convicted of an offence under section 449 450 451 or 452` IS TRUE
    `the offence attempted is punishable with death or imprisonment for life` IS FALSE
    `express provision is made by this Code or by the other written law for the punishment of the attempt` IS FALSE

-- The s 512 Illustration: an attempt to kidnap in order to murder, s 364 carrying
-- death or life.
`an attempted kidnapping to murder` MEANS `Sentencing Facts` WITH
    `the property stolen is a motor vehicle or a component part of a motor vehicle` IS FALSE
    `the robbery is committed after 7 pm and before 7 am` IS FALSE
    `the offender has previously been convicted of an offence under section 449 450 451 or 452` IS FALSE
    `the offence attempted is punishable with death or imprisonment for life` IS TRUE
    `express provision is made by this Code or by the other written law for the punishment of the attempt` IS FALSE

-- s 393 makes express provision for attempted robbery, so s 512 does not apply.
`an attempted robbery` MEANS `Sentencing Facts` WITH
    `the property stolen is a motor vehicle or a component part of a motor vehicle` IS FALSE
    `the robbery is committed after 7 pm and before 7 am` IS FALSE
    `the offender has previously been convicted of an offence under section 449 450 451 or 452` IS FALSE
    `the offence attempted is punishable with death or imprisonment for life` IS FALSE
    `express provision is made by this Code or by the other written law for the punishment of the attempt` IS TRUE

#ASSERT (`the punishment for theft`)'s `maximum imprisonment in years` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT (`the punishment for theft`)'s `fine is available`
#ASSERT NOT (`the punishment for theft`)'s `caning is available`
#ASSERT (`the punishment for theft of a motor vehicle` `a stolen car`)'s `maximum imprisonment in years` EQUALS 7
#ASSERT (`the punishment for theft of a motor vehicle` `no sentencing facts`)'s `maximum imprisonment in years` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT (`the punishment for robbery` `no sentencing facts`)'s `minimum strokes of caning` EQUALS 6
#ASSERT (`the punishment for robbery` `a night robbery`)'s `minimum strokes of caning` EQUALS 12
#ASSERT (`the punishment for robbery` `a night robbery`)'s `minimum imprisonment in years` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT (`the punishment for extortion`)'s `minimum imprisonment in years` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT (`the punishment for gang-robbery`)'s `maximum imprisonment in years` EQUALS 20
#ASSERT (`the punishment for a subsequent house-breaking offence` `a repeat house-breaker` (`imprisonment up to or fine or both` 3))'s `caning is available`
#ASSERT NOT (`the punishment for a subsequent house-breaking offence` `no sentencing facts` (`imprisonment up to or fine or both` 3))'s `caning is available`
#ASSERT (`the punishment for wrongful restraint`)'s `maximum fine in dollars` EQUALS 1500
#ASSERT (`the punishment for criminal trespass`)'s `maximum imprisonment in years` EQUALS 0.25
#ASSERT (`the punishment for infanticide`)'s `imprisonment for life is available`
#ASSERT (`the punishment for forgery`)'s `maximum imprisonment in years` EQUALS 4
#ASSERT (`the punishment for defamation`)'s `maximum imprisonment in years` EQUALS 2
-- s 512: the Illustration gives 20 years with fine or caning; an attempt with express provision is outside the section; a minimum does not bind.
#ASSERT (`the punishment for an attempt` `an attempted kidnapping to murder` `death or imprisonment for life`)'s `maximum imprisonment in years` EQUALS 20
#ASSERT NOT (`the punishment for an attempt` `an attempted kidnapping to murder` `death or imprisonment for life`)'s `death is available`
#ASSERT (`the punishment for an attempt` `an attempted robbery` (`imprisonment from to and caning of not less than strokes` 2 10 6))'s `maximum imprisonment in years` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`the punishment for an attempt` `no sentencing facts` (`imprisonment from to and caning of not less than strokes` 2 10 6))'s `minimum imprisonment in years` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`the punishment for an attempt` `no sentencing facts` (`imprisonment from to and caning of not less than strokes` 2 10 6))'s `maximum imprisonment in years` EQUALS 10
